\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus, who lived above the sky,
\par Came down to be a man and die;
\par And in the Bible we may see
\par How very good He used to be. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He went about -He was so kind-
\par To cure poor people who were blind;
\par And many who were sick and lame,
\par He pitied them and did the same.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And more than that, He told them, too,
\par The things that God would have them do;
\par And was so gentle and so mild,
\par He would have listened to a child.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. But such a cruel death He died!
\par He was hung up and crucified;
\par And those kind hands that did such good,
\par They nailed them to a cross of wood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And so He died- and this is why
\par He came to be a man and die;
\par The Bible says He came from heaven,
\par That we might have our sins forgiven.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

